# PINNED SNAPSHOT of pambase's /etc/pam.d/system-auth — AUTH section, module
# lines only (the two upstream comment lines inside the section are dropped).
#
#   source package : pambase 20260616-1
#   full-file sha256 (the whole system-auth, for the live drift sensor):
#     2bb19ead55a7b9014d107eec63cc015426c39d93ddc8af3322649ff5f8b45d5b
#   pinned         : 2026-09-05 — quickshell-auth.md, "cancel must not tally"
#
# rootfs/etc/pam.d/polkit-1 copies this section instead of `include system-auth`
# because cancelling the W auth card must not count as a failed login attempt
# (polkit ≥126 keeps the socket-activated helper alive past the cancel, and
# pam_unix answers the dead socket with PAM_CONV_ERR, which upstream system-auth
# maps to `default=bad` → pam_faillock authfail tallies it). The copy carries
# exactly ONE delta — pam_unix's control gains `conv_err=die` — and
# scripts/check/pam.sh enforces both directions: our copy matches this snapshot
# modulo that one token, and (where a live system-auth exists) the snapshot
# matches the running pambase, so a pambase update turns the gate red instead of
# silently diverging.
#
# REFRESH PROCEDURE — when check.sh --pam goes red on the live hash:
#   1. Diff the live /etc/pam.d/system-auth auth section against this fixture.
#   2. Port every upstream change into BOTH this fixture AND the copied block in
#      rootfs/etc/pam.d/polkit-1 (keeping the conv_err=die delta on pam_unix).
#   3. Update the full-file sha256 and package version in this header.
#   4. Re-run `scripts/check.sh --pam`, then re-run the characterization battery
#      on the fp VM (devtools/usr/local/bin/w-auth-cancel-probe; see
#      quickshell-auth.md) — the cancel/wrong-password/lockout branches must all
#      behave exactly as documented there.
auth       required                    pam_faillock.so      preauth
-auth      [success=2 default=ignore]  pam_systemd_home.so
auth       [success=1 default=bad]     pam_unix.so          try_first_pass nullok
auth       [default=die]               pam_faillock.so      authfail
auth       optional                    pam_permit.so
auth       required                    pam_env.so
auth       required                    pam_faillock.so      authsucc
